      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, if you look at the context of the time, switching allegiances was kind of common for guys in his position to keep their head on their shoulders. isn't it a bit unfair to judge him by modern standards of loyalty when the whole system was basically everyone for themselves? wouldn't most historians agree that his \"betrayals\" were actually just rational moves in a very unstable political climate?",
